1. rating=7.0/10 score=0.75 diff=3/5 conf=0.70 vs_base~2.50x | node_id=p2p_basic parent_id=root | Implement basic P2P path: GPU BAR buffer allocation + direct NVMe DMA — Replace the PipelineRing buffer allocation in pipeline.rs to use gpu_services::dma::create_spdk_dma_buffer_from_gpu_bar instead of host-pinned buffers. Allocate GPU memory with cuMemAlloc, then wrap as SPDK DMA buffer. Remove the cudaMemcpy H2D step from the transfer loop since DMA lands directly in GPU memory. Keep the ring structure (8 slots) and completion tracking intact.
2. rating=6.0/10 score=0.65 diff=2/5 conf=0.60 vs_base~3.50x | node_id=qd_tuning parent_id=root | Increase NVMe queue depth and in-flight I/O concurrency — After P2P path is working, increase NVMe queue depth from default to 64 and increase the number of in-flight SPDK read commands per ring slot. Use multiple SPDK I/O channels if available. This saturates the NVMe controller's internal parallelism and keeps the PCIe link busy.
3. rating=5.0/10 score=0.60 diff=2/5 conf=0.55 vs_base~3.00x | node_id=buffer_size_align parent_id=root | Optimize buffer size and alignment for P2P DMA efficiency — Tune the DMA buffer size to 2MB (aligned to hugepage boundaries) and ensure GPU allocations are 2MB-aligned for optimal TLB and BAR1 mapping efficiency. In dma.rs, use cuMemAllocHost or cuMemAlloc with explicit alignment, and set SPDK DMA buffer registration with 2MB alignment. Test 1MB vs 2MB vs 4MB buffer sizes for optimal throughput/latency tradeoff.
World Model: Chosen Next Action (from decision tree node)
- node_id: p2p_basic
- base_node_id: root
- title: Implement basic P2P path: GPU BAR buffer allocation + direct NVMe DMA
- difficulty_1_to_5: 3
- description: Replace the PipelineRing buffer allocation in pipeline.rs to use gpu_services::dma::create_spdk_dma_buffer_from_gpu_bar instead of host-pinned buffers. Allocate GPU memory with cuMemAlloc, then wrap as SPDK DMA buffer. Remove the cudaMemcpy H2D step from the transfer loop since DMA lands directly in GPU memory. Keep the ring structure (8 slots) and completion tracking intact.
- expected_vs_baseline_factor: 2.50x
- rationale: Eliminating the host bounce removes one full PCIe traversal and the cudaMemcpy latency. Expected throughput improvement from ~2.4 GB/s to ~5.5-5.9 GB/s (single drive limited). Latency drops from ~0.8ms to ~0.35ms by removing the copy stage.

