World Model: Chosen Next Action (from decision tree node)
- node_id: qd_tuning
- base_node_id: root
- title: Increase NVMe queue depth and in-flight I/O concurrency
- difficulty_1_to_5: 2
- description: After P2P path is working, increase NVMe queue depth from default to 64 and increase the number of in-flight SPDK read commands per ring slot. Use multiple SPDK I/O channels if available. This saturates the NVMe controller's internal parallelism and keeps the PCIe link busy.
- expected_vs_baseline_factor: 3.50x
- rationale: NVMe Gen4 drives achieve rated 5.9 GB/s only at QD64. If current implementation uses low QD, throughput is artificially limited. Increasing QD after P2P is in place should push throughput toward the per-drive maximum.

